Apple has <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-unveils-the-2026-designers-of-tomorrow/">showcased four design projects</a> created using its products for this year's "Designers of Tomorrow" exhibition in Paris.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-pencil-paris-design.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071857" /><br/>
The exhibition explores the theme of presence through furniture and lighting. Architect Salem S. Charabi used a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> to sketch and model a lantern, while designer Yoonjeong Lee used an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-pro/">iPad Pro</a> and the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-pencil/">Apple Pencil</a> to develop ideas for a combined table and lamp.<br/>
<br/>
Isabel Rower used an iPhone to document her work and Keynote to experiment with visual ideas for a chair featuring ceramic bead fringe. Parafernalia founders Genki Matsumura and Sebastián Zorrilla used Procreate, Messages, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a> to collaborate between Monterrey and Mexico City on a steel piece that opens into a table and stools.<br/>
<br/>
